---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { companionApps } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support"
  description="Support for Food Scanner, Glasshole, and companion apps from Scaling Human."
  path="/support.html"
>
  <article class="container prose">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="page-header__kicker">Help</p>
      <h1 class="page-header__title">Support</h1>
      <p class="page-header__lead">
        For help with Food Scanner, Glasshole, or the companion apps, contact the
        channels below.
      </p>
    </header>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: July 29, 2026</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        Email:
        <a href="mailto:srikantha.ballani@gmail.com"
          >srikantha.ballani@gmail.com</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        GitHub:
        <a
          href="https://github.com/scalinghuman/experiments"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >https://github.com/scalinghuman/experiments</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Compatibility</h2>
    <p>
      The iOS apps are iPhone apps and require iOS 26.0 or later.
    </p>
    <p>
      Glasshole supports Apple Intelligence on compatible iPhone models. Other
      supported iPhones can use configured cloud, local-network, PocketPal, or
      custom providers. Food Scanner’s default Local iPhone Vision mode works on
      supported iPhones without an API key.
    </p>

    <h2>Food Scanner</h2>
    <p>
      Food Scanner can be used without companion hardware by choosing a food
      photo from iPhone or taking a new iPhone camera photo. The optional Google
      Glass XE companion APK can capture a food image and send it to the iOS app
      over local Wi-Fi or iPhone Personal Hotspot.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Glass, open the <strong>scan food</strong> command and
      <strong>tap</strong> the touchpad to launch and capture. Do not rely on
      saying “Ok Glass.”
    </p>
    <p>
      Nutrition values are AI estimates for general information only, not medical
      advice.
    </p>

    <h2>Glasshole</h2>
    <p>
      Glasshole can be used without companion hardware by tapping the microphone
      button in the iOS app. The optional Google Glass XE companion APK can start
      and stop real-time conversation capture and display AI-powered fact-check
      overlays after analysis.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Glass, open the <strong>fact check</strong> command and
      <strong>tap</strong> the touchpad to launch, then tap again to start/stop
      listening. Do not rely on saying “Ok Glass.”
    </p>
    <p>
      Use Glasshole only with the consent of everyone being recorded and in
      compliance with local laws and regulations where you use it.
    </p>

    <h2>Common Setup (website → GitHub)</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Install the iOS app from the App Store.</li>
      <li>
        From the app page on this site (or the links below), download the
        matching companion APK:
        <a href={companionApps.foodscanner.apkUrl}>Food Scanner</a> or
        <a href={companionApps.glasshole.apkUrl}>Glasshole AI</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Follow the
        <a href={companionApps.foodscanner.guideUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Google Glass XE installation guide on GitHub</a
        >
        for ADB install, USB debugging, and hotspot setup.
      </li>
      <li>
        Connect Google Glass XE to your iPhone Personal Hotspot before opening
        the iPhone app.
      </li>
      <li>Open the iOS app and confirm the connection indicator.</li>
      <li>
        On Glass, <strong>tap</strong> the <strong>fact check</strong> or
        <strong>scan food</strong> command — do not depend on “Ok Glass” voice
        wake.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="links-row">
      <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>
      <a href="/apps/foodscanner">Food Scanner</a>
      <a href="/apps/glasshole">Glasshole AI</a>
      <a href="/">Home</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
